#: ../../../users/config.rst:5
msgid "Syncthing Configuration"
msgstr "Syncthing 組態"

#: ../../../users/config.rst:8
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:10
msgid ""
"This page covers how to configure Syncthing for file synchronization, "
"including device setup, folder configuration, connection settings, and "
"various configuration methods through the web GUI, command-line, or direct "
"file editing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:13
msgid "Configuration File Locations"
msgstr "組態檔位置"

#: ../../../users/config.rst:15
msgid "The default configuration and database directory locations are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:19
msgid ""
"$XDG_STATE_HOME/syncthing\n"
"$HOME/.local/state/syncthing\n"
"$HOME/Library/Application Support/Syncthing\n"
"%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:28
msgid "Description"
msgstr "描述"

#: ../../../users/config.rst:32
msgid ""
"The default location of the configuration and database directory on Unix-"
"like systems was changed to ``$XDG_STATE_HOME/syncthing`` or ``$HOME/.local/"
"state/syncthing``. Previously the default config location was "
"``$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/syncthing`` or ``$HOME/.config/syncthing``. The database "
"directory was previously ``$HOME/.config/syncthing`` or, if the environment "
"variable was set, ``$XDG_DATA_HOME/syncthing``. Existing installations may "
"still use these directories instead of the newer defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:43
msgid ""
"Database and config can now be set separately. Previously the database was "
"always located in the same directory as the config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:46
msgid ""
"Syncthing uses a single directory to store configuration and crypto keys. "
"Syncthing also keeps an index database with file metadata which is by "
"default stored in the same directory, though this can be overridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:50
msgid ""
"The location defaults to ``$XDG_STATE_HOME/syncthing`` or ``$HOME/.local/"
"state/syncthing`` (Unix-like), ``$HOME/Library/Application Support/"
"Syncthing`` (Mac), or ``%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Syncthing`` (Windows). It can be "
"changed at runtime using the ``--config`` or ``--home`` flags or the "
"corresponding environment variables (``$STCONFDIR`` or ``STHOMEDIR``). The "
"following files are located in this directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:57
msgid ":file:`config.xml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:58
msgid "The configuration file, in XML format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:60
msgid ":file:`cert.pem`, :file:`key.pem`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:61
msgid ""
"The device's ECDSA public and private key. These form the basis for the "
"device ID. The key must be kept private."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:64
msgid ":file:`https-cert.pem`, :file:`https-key.pem`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:65
msgid ""
"The certificate and key for HTTPS GUI connections. These may be replaced "
"with a custom certificate for HTTPS as desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:68
msgid ""
"The database is by default stored in the same directory as the config, but "
"the location may be overridden by the ``--data`` or ``--home`` flags or the "
"corresponding environment variables (``$STDATADIR`` or ``STHOMEDIR``)."
msgstr ""

