#: ../../../users/config.rst:645
msgid ""
"One or more ``device`` elements must be present in the file. Each element "
"describes a device participating in the cluster. It is customary to include "
"a ``device`` element for the local device; Syncthing will currently add one "
"if it is not present. The following attributes may be set on the ``device`` "
"element:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:655
msgid "The :ref:`device ID <device-ids>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:659
msgid "A friendly name for the device. (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:663
msgid ""
"Whether to use protocol compression when sending messages to this device. "
"The possible values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:666
msgid "``metadata``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:667
msgid ""
"Compress metadata packets, such as index information. Metadata is usually "
"very compression friendly so this is a good default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:670
msgid "``always``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:671
msgid ""
"Compress all packets, including file data. This is recommended if the "
"folders contents are mainly compressible data such as documents or text "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:675
msgid "``never``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:676
msgid "Disable all compression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:680
msgid ""
"Set to true if this device should be trusted as an introducer, i.e. we "
"should copy their list of devices per folder when connecting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:684
msgid ":doc:`introducer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:688
msgid ""
"Set to true if you wish to follow only introductions and not de-"
"introductions. For example, if this is set, we would not remove a device "
"that we were introduced to even if the original introducer is no longer "
"listing the remote device as known."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:694
msgid ""
"Defines which device has introduced us to this device. Used only for "
"following de-introductions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:698
msgid ""
"The device certificate's common name, if it is not the default \"syncthing\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:700
msgid ""
"From the following child elements at least one ``address`` child must exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:706
msgid ""
"Contains an address or host name to use when attempting to connect to this "
"device. Entries other than ``dynamic`` need a protocol specific prefix. For "
"the TCP protocol the prefixes ``tcp://`` (dual-stack), ``tcp4://`` (IPv4 "
"only) or ``tcp6://`` (IPv6 only) can be used. The prefixes for the QUIC "
"protocol are analogous: ``quic://``, ``quic4://`` and ``quic6://`` Note that "
"IP addresses need not use IPv4 or IPv6 prefixes; these are optional. "
"Accepted formats are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:712
msgid "IPv4 address (``tcp://192.0.2.42``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:713
msgid "The default port (22000) is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:715
msgid "IPv4 address and port (``tcp://192.0.2.42:12345``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:716
msgid "The address and port is used as given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:718
msgid "IPv6 address (``tcp://[2001:db8::23:42]``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:719
msgid ""
"The default port (22000) is used. The address must be enclosed in square "
"brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:722
msgid "IPv6 address and port (``tcp://[2001:db8::23:42]:12345``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:723
msgid ""
"The address and port is used as given. The address must be enclosed in "
"square brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:726
msgid "Host name (``tcp6://fileserver``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:727
msgid ""
"The host name will be used on the default port (22000) and connections will "
"be attempted only via IPv6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:730
msgid "Host name and port (``tcp://fileserver:12345``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:731
msgid ""
"The host name will be used on the given port and connections will be "
"attempted via both IPv4 and IPv6, depending on name resolution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:734
msgid "``dynamic``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:735
msgid ""
"The word ``dynamic`` (without any prefix) means to use local and global "
"discovery to find the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:738
msgid ""
"You can set multiple addresses *and* combine it with the ``dynamic`` keyword "
"for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:741
msgid ""
"<device id=\"...\">\n"
"    <address>tcp://192.0.2.1:22001</address>\n"
"    <address>quic://192.0.1.254:22000</address>\n"
"    <address>dynamic</address>\n"
"</device>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:749
msgid "In the GUI, multiple values are separated by commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:753
msgid "True if synchronization with this devices is (temporarily) suspended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:758
msgid ""
"If given, this restricts connections to this device to only this network. "
"The mechanism is described in detail in a :doc:`separate chapter </advanced/"
"device-allowednetworks>`).  To configure multiple networks, you can either: "
"repeat ``<allowedNetwork>`` tags in the configuration file or enter several "
"networks separated by commas in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:766
msgid ""
"If ``true``, folders shared from this remote device are automatically added "
"and synced locally under the :opt:`default path <defaults.folder>`.  For the "
"folder name, Syncthing tries to use the label from the remote device, and if "
"the same label already exists, it then tries to use the folder's ID.  If "
"that exists as well, the folder is just offered to accept manually.  A local "
"folder already added with the same ID will just be shared rather than "
"created separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:776
msgid ""
"Maximum send rate to use for this device. Unit is kibibytes/second, despite "
"the config name looking like kilobits/second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:781
msgid ""
"Maximum receive rate to use for this device. Unit is kibibytes/second, "
"despite the config name looking like kilobits/second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:787
msgid ""
"Contains the ID of the folder that should be ignored. This folder will "
"always be skipped when advertised from the containing remote device, i.e. "
"this will be logged, but there will be no dialog shown in the web GUI. "
"Multiple ignored folders are represented by repeated ``<ignoredFolder>`` "
"tags in the configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:795
msgid ""
"Maximum amount of data to have outstanding in requests towards this device. "
"Unit is kibibytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:800
msgid ""
"If set to a positive integer, the GUI will display an HTTP link to the IP "
"address which is currently used for synchronization.  Only the TCP port is "
"exchanged for the value specified here.  Note that any port forwarding or "
"firewall settings need to be done manually and the link will probably not "
"work for link-local IPv6 addresses because of modern browser limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:808
msgid ""
"This boolean value marks a particular device as untrusted, which disallows "
"ever sharing any unencrypted data with it.  Every folder shared with that "
"device then needs an encryption password set, or must already be of the "
"\"receive encrypted\" type locally.  Refer to the detailed explanation "
"under :doc:`untrusted`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:816
msgid ""
"The number of connections to this device. See :doc:`/advanced/device-"
"numconnections` for more information."
msgstr ""

