#: ../../../users/config.rst:1043
msgid ""
"The ``options`` element contains all other global configuration options."
msgstr "``options`` 元素包含所有其他全域組態選項。"

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1048
msgid ""
"The listen address for incoming sync connections. See :ref:`listen-"
"addresses` for the allowed syntax.  To configure multiple addresses, you can "
"either: repeat ``<listenAddress>`` tags in the configuration file or enter "
"several addresses separated by commas in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1057
msgid ""
"A URI to a global announce (discovery) server, or the word ``default`` to "
"include the default servers. Any number of globalAnnounceServer elements may "
"be present. The syntax for non-default entries is that of an HTTP or HTTPS "
"URL. A number of options may be added as query options to the URL: "
"``insecure`` to prevent certificate validation (required for HTTP URLs) and "
"``id=<device ID>`` to perform certificate pinning. The device ID to use is "
"printed by the discovery server on startup.  To configure multiple servers, "
"you can either: repeat ``<globalAnnounceServer>`` tags in the configuration "
"file or enter several servers separated by commas in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1070
msgid ""
"Whether to announce this device to the global announce (discovery) server, "
"and also use it to look up other devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1075
msgid ""
"Whether to send announcements to the local LAN, also use such announcements "
"to find other devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1080
msgid "The port on which to listen and send IPv4 broadcast announcements to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1084
msgid ""
"The group address and port to join and send IPv6 multicast announcements on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1088
msgid "Outgoing data rate limit, in kibibytes per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1092
msgid "Incoming data rate limits, in kibibytes per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1096
msgid ""
"The number of seconds to wait between each attempt to connect to currently "
"unconnected devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1101
msgid ""
"When ``true``, relays will be connected to and potentially used for device "
"to device connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1105
msgid "Sets the interval, in minutes, between relay reconnect attempts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1109
msgid ""
"Whether to attempt to start a browser to show the GUI when Syncthing starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1113
msgid ""
"Whether to attempt to perform a UPnP and NAT-PMP port mapping for incoming "
"sync connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1118
msgid ""
"Request a lease for this many minutes; zero to request a permanent lease."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1122
msgid "Attempt to renew the lease after this many minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1126
msgid "When scanning for UPnP devices, wait this long for responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1130
msgid ""
"Whether the user has accepted to submit anonymous usage data. The default, "
"``0``, mean the user has not made a choice, and Syncthing will ask at some "
"point in the future. ``-1`` means no, a number above zero means that that "
"version of usage reporting has been accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1137
msgid ""
"The highest usage reporting version that has already been shown in the web "
"GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1141
msgid ""
"The unique ID sent together with the usage report. Generated when usage "
"reporting is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1146
msgid "The URL to post usage report data to, when enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1150
msgid ""
"When true, the UR URL can be http instead of https, or have a self-signed "
"certificate. The default is ``false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1155
msgid ""
"The time to wait from startup for the first usage report to be sent. Allows "
"the system to stabilize before reporting statistics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1160
msgid ""
"Check for a newer version after this many hours. Set to ``0`` to disable "
"automatic upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1165
msgid ""
"If ``true``, automatic upgrades include release candidates (see :ref:"
"`releases`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1170
msgid ""
"Keep temporary failed transfers for this many hours. While the temporaries "
"are kept, the data they contain need not be transferred again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1175
msgid ""
"Whether to cache the results of ignore pattern evaluation. Performance at "
"the price of memory. Defaults to ``false`` as the cost for evaluating "
"ignores is usually not significant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1181
msgid ""
"How often in seconds the progress of ongoing downloads is made available to "
"the GUI. Set to ``-1`` to disable. Note that when disabled, the detailed "
"sync progress for Out of Sync Items which shows how much of each file has "
"been reused, copied, and downloaded will not work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1188
msgid ""
"Whether to apply bandwidth limits to devices in the same broadcast domain as "
"the local device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1193
msgid ""
"The minimum required free space that should be available on the partition "
"holding the configuration and index.  The element content is interpreted "
"according to the given ``unit`` attribute.  Accepted ``unit`` values are "
"``%`` (percent of the disk / volume size), ``kB``, ``MB``, ``GB`` and "
"``TB``.  Set to zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1201
msgid ""
"The URL from which release information is loaded, for automatic upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1206
msgid ""
"Network that should be considered as local given in CIDR notation.  To "
"configure multiple networks, you can either: repeat ``<alwaysLocalNet>`` "
"tags in the configuration file or enter several networks separated by commas "
"in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1213
msgid ""
"If set, device names will always be overwritten with the name given by "
"remote on each connection. By default, the name that the remote device "
"announces will only be adopted when a name has not already been set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1219
msgid ""
"When exchanging index information for incomplete transfers, only take into "
"account files that have at least this many blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1225
msgid ""
"ID of a notification to be displayed in the web GUI. Will be removed once "
"the user acknowledged it (e.g. a transition notice on an upgrade).  Multiple "
"IDs are represented by repeated ``<unackedNotificationID>`` tags in the "
"configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1232
msgid ""
"Specify an IPv4 type of service (TOS)/IPv6 traffic class for outgoing "
"packets. To specify a differentiated services code point (DSCP) the value "
"must be bit shifted to the left by two to take the two least significant ECN "
"bits into account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1240
msgid ""
"Server to use for STUN, given as ip:port. The keyword ``default`` gets "
"expanded to a set of public STUN servers, with preference given to those "
"hosted by the Syncthing project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1244
msgid ""
"To configure multiple servers, you can either: repeat ``<stunServer>`` tags "
"in the configuration file or enter several servers separated by commas in "
"the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1250
msgid ""
"Interval in seconds between contacting a STUN server to maintain NAT "
"mapping. Default is ``180`` and you can set it to ``0`` to disable "
"contacting STUN servers.  The interval is automatically reduced if needed, "
"down to a minimum of :opt:`stunKeepaliveMinS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1257
msgid "Minimum for the :opt:`stunKeepaliveStartS` interval, in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1261
msgid ""
"Syncthing will attempt to lower its process priority at startup. "
"Specifically: on Linux, set itself to a separate process group, set the "
"niceness level of that process group to nine and the I/O priority to best "
"effort level five; on other Unixes, set the process niceness level to nine; "
"on Windows, set the process priority class to below normal. To disable this "
"behavior, for example to control process priority yourself as part of "
"launching Syncthing, set this option to ``false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1271
msgid ""
"This option controls how many folders may concurrently be in I/O-intensive "
"operations such as syncing or scanning.  The mechanism is described in "
"detail in a :doc:`separate chapter </advanced/option-max-concurrency>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1278
msgid ""
"Server URL where :doc:`automatic crash reports <crashrep>` will be sent if "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1283
msgid ""
"Switch to opt out from the :doc:`automatic crash reporting <crashrep>` "
"feature. Set ``false`` to keep Syncthing from sending panic logs on serious "
"troubles.  Defaults to ``true``, to help the developers troubleshoot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1289
msgid ""
"This limits how many bytes we have \"in the air\" in the form of response "
"data being read and processed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1294
msgid ""
"Enable (the default) or disable announcing private (RFC1918) LAN IP "
"addresses to global discovery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1299
msgid ""
"Controls whether all index data is resent when an upgrade has happened, "
"equivalent to starting Syncthing with :option:`--reset-deltas`.  This used "
"to be the default behavior in older versions, but is mainly useful as a "
"troubleshooting step and causes high database churn. The default is now "
"``false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1308
msgid ""
"Feature flags are simple strings that, when added to the configuration, may "
"unleash unfinished or still-in-development features to allow early user "
"testing.  Any supported value will be separately announced with the feature, "
"so that regular users do not enable it by accident.  To configure multiple "
"flags, you can either: repeat ``<featureFlag>`` tags in the configuration "
"file or enter several flags separated by commas in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1317
msgid ""
"The number of connections at which we stop trying to connect to more "
"devices, zero meaning no limit.  Does not affect incoming connections.  The "
"mechanism is described in detail in a :doc:`separate chapter </advanced/"
"option-connection-limits>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1324
msgid ""
"The maximum number of connections which we will allow in total, zero meaning "
"no limit.  Affects incoming connections and prevents attempting outgoing "
"connections.  The mechanism is described in detail in a :doc:`separate "
"chapter </advanced/option-connection-limits>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1331
msgid ""
"When ``true``, analogous to :option:`--audit` being set. Defaults to "
"``false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1334
msgid ""
"When either this option, or :option:`--audit` (or both) are enabled, "
"auditing is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1339
msgid "Analogous to :option:`--auditfile`. Defaults to being unset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1341
msgid ""
"For compatibility reasons, if both this option and :option:`--auditfile` are "
"set, :option:`--auditfile` takes priority."
msgstr ""

