#: ../../../users/config.rst:1401
msgid ""
"The ``defaults`` element describes a template for newly added device and "
"folder options.  These will be used when adding a new remote device or "
"folder, either through the GUI or the command line interface.  The following "
"child elements can be present in the ``defaults`` element:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1408
msgid ""
"Template for a ``device`` element, with the same internal structure.  Any "
"fields here will be used for a newly added remote device.  The ``id`` "
"attribute is meaningless in this context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1414
msgid ""
"Template for a ``folder`` element, with the same internal structure.  Any "
"fields here will be used for a newly added shared folder.  The ``id`` "
"attribute is meaningless in this context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1418
msgid ""
"The UI will propose to create new folders at the path given in the ``path`` "
"attribute (used to be ``defaultFolderPath`` under ``options``).  It also "
"applies to folders automatically accepted from a remote device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1422
msgid ""
"Even sharing with other remote devices can be done in the template by "
"including the appropriate :opt:`folder.device` element underneath."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1430
msgid ""
"Template for the :ref:`ignore patterns <ignoring-files>` applied to new "
"folders.  These are copied to the ``.stignore`` file when a folder is "
"automatically accepted from a remote device.  The GUI uses them to pre-fill "
"the respective field when adding a new folder as well.  In XML, each pattern "
"line is represented as by a ``<line>`` element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1440
msgid "Listen Addresses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1442
msgid ""
"The following address types are accepted in sync protocol listen addresses. "
"If you want Syncthing to listen on multiple addresses, you can either: "
"repeat ``<listenAddress>`` tags in the configuration file or enter several "
"addresses separated by commas in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1447
msgid "Default listen addresses (``default``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1448
msgid ""
"This is equivalent to ``tcp://0.0.0.0:22000``, ``quic://0.0.0.0:22000`` and "
"``dynamic+https://relays.syncthing.net/endpoint``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1451
msgid "TCP wildcard and port (``tcp://0.0.0.0:22000``, ``tcp://:22000``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1452
msgid ""
"These are equivalent and will result in Syncthing listening on all "
"interfaces, IPv4 and IPv6, on the specified port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1455
msgid ""
"TCP IPv4 wildcard and port (``tcp4://0.0.0.0:22000``, ``tcp4://:22000``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1456
msgid ""
"These are equivalent and will result in Syncthing listening on all "
"interfaces via IPv4 only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1459
msgid "TCP IPv4 address and port (``tcp4://192.0.2.1:22000``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1460
msgid ""
"This results in Syncthing listening on the specified address and port, IPv4 "
"only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1463
msgid "TCP IPv6 wildcard and port (``tcp6://[::]:22000``, ``tcp6://:22000``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1464
msgid ""
"These are equivalent and will result in Syncthing listening on all "
"interfaces via IPv6 only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1467
msgid "TCP IPv6 address and port (``tcp6://[2001:db8::42]:22000``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1468
msgid ""
"This results in Syncthing listening on the specified address and port, IPv6 "
"only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1471
msgid "QUIC address and port (e.g. ``quic://0.0.0.0:22000``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1472
msgid ""
"Syntax is the same as for TCP, also ``quic4`` and ``quic6`` can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1474
msgid "Static relay address (``relay://192.0.2.42:22067?id=abcd123...``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/config.rst:1475
msgid ""
"Syncthing will connect to and listen for incoming connections via the "
"specified relay address."
msgstr ""

